('patient-assessment-reassessment-and-vital-signs::skills_6','patient-assessment-reassessment-and-vital-signs','patient-assessment-reassessment-and-vital-signs:skills',6,'Complete an observation of a patient using ''some teams'' – symmetry (are face and body symmetrical?), old (do they look their age?) mentation (are they alert, confused agitated or inattentive?), expression (do they appear ill, in pain or anxious?), trunk (are they thin, stocky, obese or barrel-chested?), extremities (are the fingers clubbed, are there joint abnormalities or edema?) appearance (are they clean and appropriately dressed?), movement (is their posture, gait and coordination normal, are they mobile and able to ambulate normally?) Speech (is their speech relaxed, clear, strong, understandable and appropriate, do they sound stressed?).',2006,false),
