('early-warning-signs-and-shock-emergencies::knowledge_4','early-warning-signs-and-shock-emergencies','early-warning-signs-and-shock-emergencies:knowledge',4,'Discuss the EARLY WARNING SIGNS Tool developed for area of practice and explain how the EWS Scale works.',1004,false),
('early-warning-signs-and-shock-emergencies::knowledge_5','early-warning-signs-and-shock-emergencies','early-warning-signs-and-shock-emergencies:knowledge',5,'List the NURSING INTERVENTIONS AUTHORIZED once Early Warning Signs are identified and why these are important to patient outcomes
NOTE: Patients hemodynamic status and assess airway, breathing and circulation by repeating VITAL SIGNS at least every 15 minutes.',1005,false),
('early-warning-signs-and-shock-emergencies::knowledge_6','early-warning-signs-and-shock-emergencies','early-warning-signs-and-shock-emergencies:knowledge',6,'Explain why it is necessary to ensure that the following items are ready / accessible:
• Crash cart
• Suction equipment
• Oxygen delivery
